ps you  discover the variants that allow you to  nurture your own menagerie of magical  beasts what is it  deek isn't sure  only one way to find out you can freely  customize this space to reflect your  personality and magical specialties i  mean it looks like set up a house you  have pets in there you can bring magical  creatures back and nurse them back to  health and then if you also take a  closer look from the outside here you  can see that there are other rooms or i  think they called them vivariums not  gonna lie i had to look that word up and  it means a terrarium used especially for  small animals so there you go if you  didn't know don't feel bad i didn't know  either but i think what's so awesome  about this space is it really shows they  heard the fans who were wanting this  extra level of customization that  frankly i never thought would be in the  game so this is one i think that nobody  really saw coming yes we saw the room of  requirement but having this whole sort  of extra space that we can customize and  nurse creatures back to health and is  just something that i think is a great  idea by whoever came up with that at  avalanche all right moving on to the  next one and this is certainly another  long time request of harry potter fans  and that is day and night cycles as well  as seasonal weather we're gonna lump  these two here in together as you  explore you'll find the world  surrounding hogwarts is alive with  activity wonders and areas of unusual  interest  as the school year progresses dynamic  seasons and climates will fill the sky  with lightning or sunshine or coat the  ground with snow or rain one of the  staples not only of the harry potter  movies but also of the harry potter  books is the seasons that you go through  within each novel a lot of fans can  point to specific holidays as pivotal  moments in the series i mean just in the  first book alone you have troll in the  dungeon all that happened on halloween  that christmas is when harry gets the  invisibility cloak and it was the  absolute best christmas of his life he  couldn't even believe that he woke up  and had presents and one thing the  movies really did a great job of is  showing the progression of each season  and it seems like the game is going to  follow in those same footsteps now  here's the part i am most interested  about and i haven't seen a lot of people  talking about this when it comes to the  day and night cycles and that is how  long are they actually going to be most  often in games they're going to be  simulated right it could be an hour it's  a full day but another reason that i'm a  little bit more curious about this is  because you think back to those room of  requirement menageries that we were just  talking about in there you see there are  some actual real world timers on some of  those potions at least it appears to me  to be real world timers now maybe there  are things we can earn throughout the  game that are going to speed these up i  know as soon as people saw this they  really started worrying about  microtransactions good news on that  front if you didn't know already they  have confirmed officially no micro  transactions channel wood went to  twitter and said that and then they also  have updated the official faq so no  microtransactions in hogwarts legacy  however that still leaves the question  of is this an actual real world timer  now i don't want you to think that i'm  suggesting the whole day night cycle is  tied to our real world clock similar to  something like animal crossing because i  don't think they can afford to do that  in a game like this i think we're going  to need to progress and go through  multiple days much faster however i do  wonder how they'll balance their day  night cycles with these seemingly real  world timers that we have here now  another thing i've also seen people talk  about is that seasons almost has to be  confirmation that we will be getting  multiple school years at hogwarts rather  than just the fifth year which is what  i've kind of been thinking for a while  now now i actually love this line of  thinking i mean it kind of makes sense  right which you really want to program  seasonal weather in for just having it  change one time but here's the tricky  part and it relates directly back to the  day night cycles you see they control  how long these are and so how long these  days are really is what sets the overall  length of the game if you think about it  because games have to find some way to  show that progression of time without  having you actually sit there through  every single hour every single minute of  the day animal crossing is a rarity in  that and then the other big thing we  don't know about the day night cycles is  how do you progress them so is it  actually a timer and you're sneaking  around the castle at night and you could  actually run out of time like you could  stay out all night and then morning  starts to rise and you have to get to  class is that how it works or is it  similar to what the older games and even  what some more current games have done  in that you actually have to progress to  the next day so it will stay night for  many real world hours if you want to and  then you choose when it's time to  progress it is that how it works and see  that's what i think is so interesting  about this how are they going to  approach this because you think about a  game like breath of the wild link  doesn't have to worry about going back  to a school to go to different classes  that are set at different times  throughout the day he can just roam the  world freely as much as he wants so the  sun rises sun sets it rains it snows and  he's just running around doesn't matter  he doesn't have anyone else to kind of  report back to right whereas in the  hogwarts legacy we do have that  connection back to the school and these  classes i'm sure they'll handle it in a  very elegant way i just think that's a  big question that we really still don't  know the answer to regardless i am super  pumped super excited that day night  cycles are in as well as the seasonal  weather changes i think it's going to be  fantastic for the overall feel of the  game all right for the next one let's  jump back to yet another one that a lot  of people were asking for and that is  customizable gear they showed that shot  in hogsmeade of our character being able  to go into different shops purchase all  sorts of different items and then they  showed this little sequence right here  where we can see all this different gear  that we can put on our character this is  something again that people have been  asking for for a while now one thing  they did not show that you guys are  super interested in and that is the idea  of a customizable wand customizable  wands that is something i see so often  in the comments and i've just been going  and responding to everyone saying the  wand chooses the wizard it's not always  clear why but in all seriousness i would  like to see this i wouldn't have a huge  problem with it i know it kind of would  break the canon a little bit because of  the fact that the way it works in the  world is you really don't get to choose  your wand the wand chooses you now maybe  once you have the wand i don't know if  you want to like make certain carvings  in it if you want to like put little  ribbons on it if you want to paint part  of it a different color maybe those  things they could figure out a way to  work in there or maybe you have sort of  like the base one and then you can just  customize things like the handle i do  think there are ways they could make it  work and still stay relatively true to  the harry potter lore okay real quick  before we get to the last one i have to  give some honorable mentions because  there were just so many epic moments for  long time fans in this gameplay trailer  i couldn't not talk about the house  elves in the kitchens i love seeing this  shot we've imagined this in our heads  but we've never been able to see it on  screen because the movies did not  include the house elves in the kitchen  so i love that they did this i just want  to go hang out in here and sit with  these house elves and listen to what  they talk about throughout the day maybe  we can even get side quests and things  from them another big one the prefix  bathroom they absolutely nailed this you  have all the fun little knobs they even  put the diving board in there and then  our final honorable mention is the house  common rooms they did a fantastic job  with gryffindor and slytherin but it's  the ravenclaw and hufflepuff common  rooms that everyone is talking about  because of how little we have seen of  them we never saw them in the movies in  the books harry goes to the ravenclaw  common room but the hufflepuff common  room first time any of us ever seen it  and i know a lot of the hufflepuff folks  out there were super pumped for that so  just seeing those common rooms even  though it was such a short glimpse we  could see the attention to detail we  could see how different and how true to  each house they made those so those  three honorable mentions there i just  could not in the video without talking  about them and then last but certainly  not least this one was not even  mentioned in the gameplay trailer at all  this actually happened after the fact  and it was almost like they were trying  to hide this i don't understand why they  didn't make a bigger deal about this but  that is the fact that hogwarts legacy is  coming to the nintendo switch guys i  made a video months and months and  months ago about hey i wonder if they're  going to actually not bring the games to  last gen if they're going to make this  just next gen only so drop the ps4  version no in fact they're taking it a  step further they're going to say it's  on anything and everything pc xbox  playstation nintendo switch wherever you  wanna play if you have a fairly recent  gaming console or one of the new gaming  consoles or a pc you will be able to  play hogwarts legacy in fact if you're  in the us i know for sure that  pre-orders have opened up i'll put a  link down in the description below if  you're in other parts of the world and  interested in pre-ordering keep an eye  out because they have been popping up at  various retailers now as i always  caution people pre-ordering is entirely  up to you i am personally waiting  because i am holding out hope that we  get a collector's edition at this point  we don't know about that yet so those  for me guys were the five biggest  reveals but i want to hear from you what  was your favorite reveal of the new  gameplay trailer let me know in the  comments below as always thank you all  so much for watching  i'll talk to you again soon

